[{:db/id 17592186105911 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b1d14526-d850-5fde-b6de-399e3114c554" "question-7183bcde-c002-5fb8-96a6-052694ff64b0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105486 :question/problem "Find an expression that's equivalent to $\\dfrac{2}3 a.$" :question/worked-solution "Writing $a$ as $\\dfrac{a}{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\,a & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot a \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{a}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot a}{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2a}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expressions $\\dfrac{2}{3}a$ and $\\dfrac{2a}{3}$ are equivalent." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105835 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bc5db206-5120-5419-9d82-dc30e18e3280" "question-c402ae86-03e2-521f-97be-fa33095984c9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105683 :question/problem "Find an  expression  equivalent to $-\\dfrac{2}9 (-z).$" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that the product of two negative numbers is a positive number. Thus, \n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{2}9 (-z) = \\dfrac{2}{9} z.\n$$\n\nNow, writing $z$ as $\\dfrac{z}{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}z & =\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot z \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{z}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot z}{9\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2z}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expressions $-\\dfrac{2}9 (-z)$ and $\\dfrac{2z}{9}$ are equivalent." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105910 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1e7a5473-d897-50f6-be12-c307a084dd8c" "question-15c1975a-5c77-59ea-b22f-26a9fa9a40fc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105485 :question/worked-solution "Writing $y-3$ as $\\dfrac{y-3}{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{7}\\,(y-3) & =\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot (y-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot \\frac{y-3}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (y-3)}{7\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y-6}{7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105912 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8c6ba30d-a56f-524d-91ab-97b68e7f3806" "question-b7c9d305-cc80-564f-85ac-61aa6b7be138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105487 :question/problem "Find an expression equivalent to $\\dfrac{2(3-x)}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Pulling out the variable part, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(3-x)}{5} & =\\frac{2\\cdot (3-x)}{5\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{3-x}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot (3-x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(3-x)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1d14526-d850-5fde-b6de-399e3114c554" :question/id #uuid "b1d14526-d850-5fde-b6de-399e3114c554" :question/math-academy-id "q-70072" :question/problem "The expression $\\frac{4}{9}z$ is equivalent to" :question/worked-solution "Writing $z$ as $\\frac{z}{1}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{9}z & =\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot z \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot \\frac{z}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot z}{9\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4z}{9}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expressions $\\frac{4}{9}z$ and $\\frac{4z}{9}$ are equivalent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7678abef-6fc9-566f-a3d2-51bceb099136"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7678abef-6fc9-566f-a3d2-51bceb099136" :answer-field/id #uuid "7678abef-6fc9-566f-a3d2-51bceb099136" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eb0d942f-6012-5fcf-8917-500064bac3a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb0d942f-6012-5fcf-8917-500064bac3a6" "answer-d6d5c43c-a38c-5f1a-a320-c93bef4c2f1f" "answer-3e1a787f-eb02-5d88-933c-83c817fe3424" "answer-db15d214-8a1c-5cb2-82df-4c71d1c53c63" "answer-034efbf9-242f-5b63-b5dd-f4db2ff21b37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb0d942f-6012-5fcf-8917-500064bac3a6" :answer/id #uuid "eb0d942f-6012-5fcf-8917-500064bac3a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4z}{9}" :db/ensure [