value "\\frac{2R+2}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3af6fa54-b458-57c0-bbd5-da3fd4023122" :answer/id #uuid "3af6fa54-b458-57c0-bbd5-da3fd4023122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2R+2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c58ed31-7000-5ada-9259-4e1d67dd03e2" :answer/id #uuid "8c58ed31-7000-5ada-9259-4e1d67dd03e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{R+2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8c6ba30d-a56f-524d-91ab-97b68e7f3806" :question/id #uuid "8c6ba30d-a56f-524d-91ab-97b68e7f3806" :question/math-academy-id "q-70084" :question/problem "$\\frac{q}{8}$ is equivalent to" :question/worked-solution "Pulling out the variable part, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{q}{8} & =\\frac{1\\cdot q}{8\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{q}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot q \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\,q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d4bcf16-d35c-5fb5-a3d3-abc4106846f0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d4bcf16-d35c-5fb5-a3d3-abc4106846f0" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d4bcf16-d35c-5fb5-a3d3-abc4106846f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-02c245ff-1482-52e4-bae8-ae7027d33cf0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eca40d4f-0ca8-577f-9212-35bf9417f2d2" "answer-806af50c-a985-5b05-ad91-4722d5532c0e" "answer-1e025295-ad73-5e33-ab2f-f48cf29b6ba5" "answer-02c245ff-1482-52e4-bae8-ae7027d33cf0" "answer-3515399b-d41a-5057-8485-9428f04cbf49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eca40d4f-0ca8-577f-9212-35bf9417f2d2" :answer/id #uuid "eca40d4f-0ca8-577f-9212-35bf9417f2d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8q}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-806af50c-a985-5b05-ad91-4722d5532c0e" :answer/id #uuid "806af50c-a985-5b05-ad91-4722d5532c0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}+q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e025295-ad73-5e33-ab2f-f48cf29b6ba5" :answer/id #uuid "1e025295-ad73-5e33-ab2f-f48cf29b6ba5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}-q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02c245ff-1482-52e4-bae8-ae7027d33cf0" :answer/id #uuid "02c245ff-1482-52e4-bae8-ae7027d33cf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\,q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3515399b-d41a-5057-8485-9428f04cbf49" :answer/id #uuid "3515399b-d41a-5057-8485-9428f04cbf49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "q-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b7c9d305-cc80-564f-85ac-61aa6b7be138" :question/id #uuid "b7c9d305-cc80-564f-85ac-61aa6b7be138" :question/math-academy-id "q-108701" :question/problem "Find an expression equivalent to $\\frac{5(h-7)}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Pulling out the variable part, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5(h-7)}{3} & =\\frac{5\\cdot (h-7)}{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{h-7}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot (h-7) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}(h-7)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e538b378-3b69-56c5-ba57-e6cbee09c67e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e538b378-3b69-56c5-ba57-e6cbee09c67e" :answer-field/id #uuid "e538b378-3b69-56c5-ba57-e6cbee09c67e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f3ba6131-3d4c-5d31-b82c-11420617b643" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5e04d72-6333-5423-8a26-be3f7c87b38a" "answer-f3ba6131-3d4c-5d31-b82c-11420617b643" "answer-64048473-c43e-50d6-97ba-5a502bb393c8" "answer-1c828ca6-478f-5d13-b730-03b546f17d19" "answer-fa0eeda1-b4fa-59c1-8266-fac7db871771"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5e04d72-6333-5423-8a26-be3f7c87b38a" :answer/id #uuid "c5e04d72-6333-5423-8a26-be3f7c87b38a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5h}{3}-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3ba6131-3d4c-5d31-b82c-11420617b643" :answer/id #uuid "f3ba6131-3d4c-5d31-b82c-11420617b643" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}(h-7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64048473-c43e-50d6-97ba-5a502bb393c8" :answer/id #uuid "64048473-c43e-50d6-97ba-5a502bb393c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{7}{h-7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c828ca6-478f-5d13-b730-03b546f17d19" :answer/id #uuid "1c828ca6-478f-5d13-b730-03b546f17d19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{h}-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa0eeda1-b4fa-59c1-8266-fac7db871771" :answer/id #uuid "fa0eeda1-b4fa-59c1-8266-fac7db871771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{h}{3(h-7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186107032 :tutorial/content "Two expressions involving fractions are **equivalent** if they are the same.\n\nEven if two expressions initially appear different, they might still be equivalent. For example, the expressions $\\dfrac{1}{2}x$ and $\\dfrac{x}{2}$ both represent the same thing: \"half of $x.$\" Consequently, they are equivalent.\n\nWe can also see that these expressions are equivalent because $\\dfrac{1}{2}x$ can be transformed into $\\dfrac{x}{2}.$ Writing $x$ as $\\dfrac{x}{1},$ we can multiply $\\dfrac 1 2$ and $\\dfrac x 1$ using fraction multiplication, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot x}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186107033 :tutorial/content "The usual procedure also works in the reverse direction. For example, to find an equivalent expression for $\\dfrac{2(y+1)}5,$ we can separate the variable part from the rest of the fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(y+1)}{5} & =\\frac{2\\cdot (y+1)}{5\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{(y+1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot (y+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\,(y+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105969 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
